  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 4.5,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To the rider and to the driver: this is about the SGD 4.50 no-show fee charged on trip TRP-03204 (EV-FARE-03204: cancellation_fee 4.50, total_charged 4.50, payment_status CHARGED). I am refunding it in full to the rider and paying the driver nothing.\n\nThe driver's side of the case is first made out, and I accept it. EV-TRIP-03204 shows the driver tapped 'I'm Here' at 13:17:57, the wait timer started two seconds later, and the driver cancelled at 13:24:38 under reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW. EV-GPS-03204 places the driver at 41 qualifying fixes inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius from 13:17:57 to 13:24:37 - one continuous 400-second dwell, measured from the first in-geofence fix, against the 180-second free waiting period in force (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec). The arrival marker was not false: the first qualifying fix falls at 13:17:57 itself (dwell_start_offset_sec 0.0) and the driver was stationary, not travelling at 15 km/h or more, so POL-NS-05 does not fire and the 400-second dwell stands. POL-NS-06 shows no shortfall: the measured dwell is 220 seconds over the minimum and run_count is 1, so there is no second in-geofence interval for anyone to sum. POL-NS-01(d) is met - no boarding event, terminated by the driver under RIDER_NO_SHOW, 221 seconds after the required dwell elapsed, with no_show_threshold_sec null. The fare line reconciles: 4.50 equals platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd, so there is no POL-NS-08(d) fare defect.\n\nNone of that saves the fee, because POL-NS-04 applies and all three of its limbs hold. (a) Inside the waiting window the rider sent three messages (EV-CHAT-03204: 13:18:27, 13:19:47 and 13:20:27); the first asks which car the driver is in and says she cannot see him, which is exactly the locating-or-coordinating content limb (a) describes. (b) The log holds no driver message at all, so nothing was posted within 120 seconds of any of those messages, and trip_record.in_app_calls is an empty array, so no in-app call was placed before the driver ended the trip. Opening a message is not replying: MSG-03204-003 was read at 13:20:07 and the driver still wrote nothing and called no one before cancelling at 13:24:38. (c) The rider's own track in EV-GPS-03204 places her device between 15.07 m and 22.11 m from the pickup pin across 68 fixes spanning 13:15:58 to 13:26:00 - every qualifying fix well inside the 100 m STANDARD rider presence radius. A driver who serves his clock but cancels on a rider who is at the pin and signalling that she cannot find him has not completed the pickup, and POL-NS-04 refunds the fee in full and says no driver compensation is payable. The driver's figure of SGD 3.60 (EV-FARE-03204 derived.money.driver_compensation, 80 per cent of 4.50) is therefore not paid: POL-NS-07 pays only where no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces POL-NS-01, and POL-NS-04 does. For completeness, the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check would not have tripped in any event - no_show_terminations_30d is 0 and completed_trips_30d is 118 - and I have not used prior_no_show_flags, a context-only lifetime counter.\n\nTwo driver points I do not accept. First, the rider's mention of 'the taxi stand near Lim Chu Kang Road side' does not undo limb (a): that limb turns on whether the message is locating or coordinating, and it plainly is, and the wording cannot be used to place her away from the pin when her own track puts her 15 to 22 m from it - no party may assert that a named place is or is not the same venue on general knowledge (POL-NS-03). Second, the chat log header shows last_message_at 13:19:47 while MSG-03204-002 is sent at 13:20:27; that is a header inconsistency, but it is not a POL-NS-08(c) defect, because the msg_id sequence 001 to 003 is intact and the log holds 3 messages, matching trip_record.chat_message_count of 3.\n\nNothing here needs a human reviewer. The trace is COMPLETE at weight 1.0 with 100.0 per cent coverage, zero gaps and both tracks present; the chat log and trip record are COMPLETE at weight 1.0; the fare breakdown reconciles; so no POL-NS-08 limb (a) to (d) is engaged and no POL-NS-09 trigger fires. The missing traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-03204-01 (weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT) carries no fact and is moot - the rider disclosed it correctly, and with a single 400-second run there is no second interval for an advisory to permit anyone to sum. Confidence is 0.90: every artifact that carries the deciding facts - the chat log, the GPS trace and the trip record - is COMPLETE at weight 1.0, so nothing discounts the finding. The monetary effect, SGD 4.50, is below the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of SGD 8.00, so this refund executes automatically. No clause produces a referral on these facts: the arrival marker was true, the anti-farming check does not trip, and the reason code used is one POL-NS-01(d) recognises."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

